u003c/div\\u003e\\n\\u003cimg alt=\\\&quot;\\\&quot; width=\\\&quot;24\\\&quot; height=\\\&quot;24\\\&quot; src=\\\&quot;https://doy2mn9upadnk.cloudfront.net/user_avatar/devforum.roblox.com/luckyraingg/60/6868043_2.png\\\&quot; class=\\\&quot;avatar\\\&quot;\\u003e LuckyRainGG:\\u003c/div\\u003e\\n\\u003cblockquote\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003cstrong\\u003ePublishing vs. Saving Requirements\\u003c/strong\\u003e: We’ve made version notes required when you publish to help you keep track of what went live to your players.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003c/blockquote\\u003e\\n\\u003c/aside\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003eI do like this feature, I personally neglect all the time to document what I’m doing and so I’ll often just forget what I changed in some version from months ago, so having a reminder to write version notes for published versions is nice. With that being said this should still probably be an optional setting in Studio given that a lot of people either don’t really care much or document changes elsewhere anyways, also for people working in a test place having to write notes on every publish is probably going to get pretty annoying pretty quickly.\\u003c/p\\u003e\&quot;,\&quot;post_number\&quot;:43,\&quot;post_type\&quot;:1,\&quot;posts_count\&quot;:141,\&quot;updated_at\&quot;:\&quot;2026-02-28T02:51:58.555Z\&quot;,\&quot;reply_count\&quot;:0,\&quot;reply_to_post_number\&quot;:null,\&quot;quote_count\&quot;:1,\&quot;incoming_link_count\&quot;:4,\&quot;reads\&quot;:542,\&quot;readers_count\&quot;:541,\&quot;score\&quot;:188.4,\&quot;yours\&quot;:false,\&quot;topic_id\&quot;:4451086,\&quot;topic_slug\&quot;:\&quot;redesigned-place-version-history-in-studio\&quot;,\&quot;display_username\&quot;:\&quot;YuNoGuy123\&quot;,\&quot;primary_group_name\&quot;:null,\&quot;flair_name\&quot;:\&quot;Programmers\&quot;,\&quot;flair_url\&quot;:\&quot;scroll\&quot;,\&quot;flair_bg_color\&quot;:\&quot;0043FF\&quot;,\&quot;flair_color\&quot;:\&quot;fff\&quot;,\&quot;flair_group_id\&quot;